[[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Raise the rear seat cushion.</p><p>2. Undo the bolts fixing the running board.</p><p>3. Remove the running board.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005351.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the kick plate is\nundamaged.</p><p>Position the running board and secure it\nusing the bolts.</p><p>Lower the rear seat cushion.</p>"]]